// fcpwb-gpu-parallel.bonsai's launch made through OptiX: every (walk, point)
// pair is a thread of one ray-generation launch -- `bind(k, OptixThread)`,
// the loop's body the raygen program of an OptiX module of its own
// (docs/schedule-semantics.md, 3; CodeGen_OptiX) -- with no query on the
// ray tracing hardware: the distance query is the kernel's software
// traversal of FCPW's tree, as in every schedule of this table. OptiX
// chooses the launch's block shape; nothing else differs from the plain
// launch. Against fcpwb-gpu-parallel it measures what the OptiX launch
// itself costs or gives, and it is the control for fcpwb-gpu-optix-ser,
// which adds the one thing only such a launch can have: the threads
// reordered between the steps.
import apps/wosx/schedules/kernel/fcpwb;

schedule {
    solve_all.reorder(i, w);
    solve_all.collapse(w, i, k);
    solve_all.bind(k, OptixThread);
}
